#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:42
msgid ""
"Why are my pods failing with a ``CrashLoopBackOff`` error after adding a "
"custom CA certificate to my Docker image?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:44
msgid ""
"You may see a ``CrashLoopBackOff`` error after adding a custom CA "
"certificate to your Docker image's ``/etc/ssl/certs`` directory and "
"deploying it to your Kubernetes environment via the Mattermost Enterprise"
" Edition Helm Chart. This issue typically arises because the custom CA "
"certificate is not being recognized by the system's certificate trust "
"store, leading to TLS handshake failures when the application attempts to"
" connect to services that require the custom CA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:46
msgid ""
"While core functionality may remain operational, you may notice the "
"following symptoms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:48
msgid ""
"Pods stuck in a crashloop with the error message: backoff - restarting "
"failed container in pod."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:49
msgid ""
"Debugging commands like ``kubectl describe`` and ``kubectl logs`` provide"
" little to no valuable information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:50
msgid "Integrations may be blocked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:53
msgid "Can I resolve this issue without rebuilding the Docker image?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:55
msgid ""
"Yes. We recommend using Kubernetes-native solutions to manage custom CA "
"certificates to simplify deployment processes and minimize disruptions "
"caused by image rebuilds. You can inject the certificate directly into "
"the pod using Kubernetes resources instead of modifying the Docker image "
"to manage custom CA certificates dynamically without needing to rebuild "
"and redeploy your Docker image every time the certificate changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:57
msgid ""
"Use a Kubernetes secret to store your custom CA certificate and then "
"mount it into the pod:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:59
msgid "Create a Kubernetes secret with your custom CA certificate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:60
msgid ""
"Mount the certificate into the pod using the Helm chart’s configuration "
"options. This method simplifies management and avoids the need to rebuild"
" your Docker image for future certificate updates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:62
msgid ""
"Alternatively, to dynamically inject certificates without modifying the "
"Docker image, use an ``initContainer`` to copy the certificate into the "
"pod's filesystem and update the certificate trust store before the main "
"container starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:65
msgid "How to troubleshoot the root cause of the ``CrashLoopBackOff`` error?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:67
msgid "Use ``kubectl describe pods`` to check detailed event logs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:69
msgid ""
"Consider logging tools like Grafana to aggregate and analyze logs for "
"additional insights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:72
msgid "Where is data stored in a self-hosted Kubernetes deployment?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:74
msgid ""
"Where data is stored depends on the backend database (such as RDS, Azure "
"Postgres, self-hosted PostgreSQL), and the backend filestore (such as AWS"
" S3, other S3-compatible services, or a mounted volume) configured during"
" deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:76
msgid ""
"For volume mounts, we recommend using an NFS volume to provide filestores"
" as a \"local\" directory to the Mattermost server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/deploy-kubernetes.rst:78
msgid ""
"Not all types of `Kubernetes persistent volumes "
"<https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/persistent-volumes/#types-"
"of-persistent-volumes>`_ have been tested with Mattermost, and some may "
"have limitations or specific configurations that may require additional "
"setup to ensure proper permissions and access. We recommend system admins"
" review documentation for their preferred persistent volume types and "
"test to ensure compatibility with Mattermost."
msgstr ""

